From 41f48e826a221811187b26d59ed31e653e550e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:29:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/76] e2_memstats r5: boundary-only telemetry, no polling
 inside a measured region

The r2/r3 hook read memory_stats() and reset_peak_memory_stats() every VLLM_E2_MEMSTATS
seconds. Both take the per-device caching-allocator mutex and the Python bindings do not
release the GIL, so the preregistered claim that this thread takes no lock shared with the
model path was false. Three one-boot arms at pin 4.1e9 showed a monotone dose-response:
4 Hz wedged a stage-0 worker during A-think-131072, 1.1 Hz survived that row and wedged
during A-think-260000, and with the thread disabled the run completed every row.
Causation is not established at n=1 per arm, but polling has no place inside a measured
region and was never necessary - PyTorch maintains the allocator high-water marks itself.

Between boundaries the thread now makes NO CUDA call: its tick is a plain read of
window.ctl. At a boundary, which the driver crosses only while the server is quiet, it
does exactly one allocator interaction - memory_stats, reset_peak_memory_stats
immediately after with no file I/O in the gap, then mem_get_info - and writes the close
and ack records. No sample records exist any more, and the evaluator rejects any it sees.

Declared loss of resolution: peaks are exact per ROW window, not per P3F interval.
